Steve Brooks
Schooling: He attended Christchurch Boys' High School from 2001 to 2003. He was highly entrepreneurial from a very early age, famously becoming New Zealand’s youngest real estate agent at age 14 and making his first million by 19. [1, 2, 3]
Where He Lives: He is based in Christchurch, Canterbury. [1, 2]
Family: While specific details about his immediate family are kept relatively private, it is noted that he and business partner James Cooney are close friends who regularly share family holidays together. [1]


James Cooney
Schooling: He attended Sacred Heart College for secondary school and went on to study at Lincoln University, graduating in 2009 with a Bachelor of Commerce in Valuation and Property Management.
Where He Lives: He is based in Christchurch, New Zealand.
Family: He is married to his wife, Alice Cooney, and they have a young family together. [1, 2]

(Note: In 2026, the two founders amicably split their massive $800 million Wolfbrook Property Group portfolio to focus on their respective business passions; James Cooney retained ownership of the residential development side, Wolfbrook Residential.) [1, 2]
